  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Server Setup**\n\nOkay, I\'m examining the `server.ts` file now. It looks like it handles running Express with Vite middlewares during development using `tsx server.ts`, and also serves the `/dist` folder in production. I\'ve also noted the `/api/proxy` endpoint, which is used for forwarding HTTP/HTTPS requests to the Daidai Panel when needed. I\'m checking it further.\n\n\n**Evaluating Proxy Benefit**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about the benefits of the `/api/daidai-proxy` endpoint. It\'s becoming clearer why it\'s so helpful, specifically in cases where the Daidai panel is HTTP, and the app is on HTTPS, like when deployed on Cloud Run. The proxy bypasses mixed-content errors in the browser, making the setup much more robust for remote testing. This design choice is looking really solid.\n\n\n**Implementing Proxy Fallback**\n\nI\'m working on robustifying the fetch mechanism. The idea is, if a direct fetch fails due to CORS or mixed-content errors, the app will automatically try `/api/daidai-proxy`. There\'s also a user toggle for this functionality, \"\346\234\215\345\212\241\347\253\257\344\273\243\347\220\206 (\347\273\225\350\277\207\350\267\250\345\237\237\344\270\216Mixed Content)\", which increases the app\'s versatility in different network settings. I\'m exploring the `server.ts` file, and `package.json` now. Specifically, I\'m adjusting the scripts in `package.json`, focusing on the `\"dev\"` and `\"start\"` commands, and thinking about how to seamlessly integrate the proxy into the development workflow using `tsx server.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining Proxy Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of the `/api/daidai-proxy` endpoint. I\'ve noted it handles POST requests. It extracts the `targetUrl`, `method`, `headers`, and `body` from the request. Then, I\'m analyzing how it constructs a fetch request, including removing the \'host\' header. Finally, it properly handles the response, whether JSON or text, and forwards it to the client. The goal is to make it robust and fault-tolerant.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_470063"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import express from \'express\';\\nimport dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\nimport path from \'path\';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\\n\\ndotenv.config();\\n\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\\n\\nconst app = express();\\nconst port = parseInt(process.env.PORT || \'3000\', 10);\\n\\napp.use(express.json({ limit: \'10mb\' }));\\n\\n// Health check endpoint\\napp.get(\'/api/health\', (_req, res) => {\\n  res.json({ status: \'ok\', timestamp: Date.now() });\\n});\\n\\n// Daidai Panel CORS & Mixed Content Proxy endpoint\\napp.post(\'/api/daidai-proxy\', async (req, res) => {\\n  try {\\n    const { targetUrl, method = \'GET\', headers = {}, body } = req.body;\\n    if (!targetUrl || typeof targetUrl !== \'string\') {\\n      return res.status(400).json({ code: 400, message: \'Missing targetUrl\' });\\n    }\\n\\n    const fetchHeaders: Record<string, string> = { ...headers };\\n    delete fetchHeaders[\'host\'];\\n\\n    const response = await fetch(targetUrl, {\\n      method,\\n      headers: fetchHeaders,\\n      body: body ? (typeof body === \'string\' ? body : JSON.stringify(body)) : undefined,\\n    });\\n\\n    const contentType = response.headers.get(\'content-type\') || \'\';\\n    if (contentType.includes(\'application/json\')) {\\n      const data = await response.json();\\n      return res.status(response.status).json(data);\\n    } else {\\n      const text = await response.text();\\n      return res.status(response.status).send(text);\\n    }\\n  } catch (err: unknown) {\\n    const errorMessage = err instanceof Error ? err.message : \'\347\275\221\347\273\234\350\277\236\346\216\245\350\266\205\346\227\266\346\210\226\347\233\256\346\240\207\345\234\260\345\235\200\344\270\215\345\217\257\350\276\276\';\\n    return res.status(502).json({\\n      code: 502,\\n      message: `\344\273\243\347\220\206\350\257\267\346\261\202\345\244\261\350\264\245: ${errorMessage}`,\\n    });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\n// Mount Vite in development or serve static build in production\\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV !== \'production\') {\\n  const { createServer } = await import(\'vite\');\\n  const vite = await createServer({\\n    server: {\\n      middlewareMode: true,\\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\\n    },\\n    appType: \'spa\',\\n  });\\n  app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n} else {\\n  app.use(express.static(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\')));\\n  app.get(\'*\', (_req, res) => {\\n    res.sendFile(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\', \'index.html\'));\\n  });\\n}\\n\\napp.listen(port, \'0.0.0.0\', () => {\\n  console.log(`Server listening on http://0.0.0.0:${port}`);\\n});\\n\", \"Description\":\"Server entry point with Express, Vite middlewares and proxy endpoint\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing file\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create server.ts\"}"
