  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the application modules. I\'ve begun defining the core data structures, starting with `src/types/index.ts`. My initial approach involves specifying the `PanelConfig` type, which includes parameters like `apiUrl`, `appKey`, `appSecret`, and `targetEnvName` to ensure clean and flexible application design.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the specific data structures. I\'ve defined `PanelConfig`, `SyncRecord`, and `EnvItem`, along with their associated properties. I\'m focusing on attributes like `remarks`, `autoReadOnLaunch`, and `useProxy`. I\'m also considering how to structure the `SyncRecord` to capture important details about synchronization events, including status, duration, and content summaries.\n\n\n**Mapping API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now detailing the API interactions. I\'ve mapped out endpoints like `/api/v1/open-api/token`, its payload and expected response, and endpoints for testing connections, fetching environments, and syncing environments. I\'ve also outlined how to handle existing versus new environment scenarios and the corresponding API calls, like `PUT` and `POST` for synchronization processes.\n\n\n**Developing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve progressed to integrating the React components. I\'m actively working on UI elements like the `Navbar` with its connection badge and PWA install prompt. The `WorkspaceView` is taking shape too, with a large clipboard trigger card that offers both clipboard read functionality and manual paste. I\'m also implementing the live preview card, which includes character/line count and masking controls, and the target variable indicator card to edit the target variable name. I\'m focusing on user interaction and dynamic updates. I\'m using `useClipboard.ts` hook for graceful clipboard management and `usePWAInstall.ts` hook for detecting and managing PWA installation.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Updates**\n\nI\'m now integrating the primary action button with a floating, touch-optimized CTA for immediate updates, including haptic feedback during loading. I\'m also adding a quick result banner to show execution details. I\'m building out the `HistoryView`, displaying past sync operations, and implementing re-send, copy, and clear actions. I\'m also building `EnvsListView` for displaying and quick selection of variables. Lastly, I\'m working on the `SettingsView`.\n\n\n"
